  // your own battles before playing with it. Off: what it decides happens.
  // (true or false)
  "ImpactShadowMode": false,

  // The highest chance that a kick or bash makes a man drop the shield in his hand - reached
  // when he is exhausted or badly outmatched. 0 in the green between even men.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "KickShieldDropMaxPercent": 90,

  // The highest chance that a kick or bash knocks a man to the ground.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "KickKnockdownMaxPercent": 80,

  // The highest chance that a man who blocks a blow with his shield on the RIGHT side staggers
  // back - reached only on a BIG mismatch (his own tiredness counts as little as the
  // correct-block setting below says), longer the more tired he is.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "RightBlockStaggerMaxPercent": 30,

  // The highest chance that a RIGHT-side shield block makes him drop his shield. 0: a clean
  // block is the reward for skill - only kicks and wrong-side blocks drop shields.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "RightBlockShieldDropMaxPercent": 0,

  // The highest chance that a RIGHT-side shield block still knocks him down - a huge mismatch
  // (a peasant's stick against a berserker's axe), hardly his own tiredness.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "RightBlockKnockdownMaxPercent": 10,

  // The highest chance that a man who parries a blow with his weapon staggers back - a parry is
  // a correct block: reached only on a BIG mismatch.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "ParryStaggerMaxPercent": 30,

  // The highest chance that a parry still knocks the parrying man down - a huge mismatch,
  // hardly his own tiredness.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "ParryKnockdownMaxPercent": 10,

  // The highest chance that a man who blocks with his shield on the WRONG side staggers back.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "WrongBlockStaggerMaxPercent": 90,

  // The highest chance that a WRONG-side shield block makes him drop his shield.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "WrongBlockShieldDropMaxPercent": 50,

  // The highest chance that a WRONG-side shield block knocks him down.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "WrongBlockKnockdownMaxPercent": 40,

  // The highest chance that a blow that lands unblocked staggers a man longer than the game's
  // own flinch.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "HitStaggerMaxPercent": 80,

  // The highest chance that a blow that lands unblocked knocks a man down.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "HitKnockdownMaxPercent": 50,

  // The highest chance that a right-side block or parry staggers the ATTACKER - for an empty or
  // outmatched attacker swinging into a good guard: a tired man flailing into a correct block
  // opens himself up, whoever holds it (the next setting lets the blocker's own tiredness lower
  // it).
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "RiposteStaggerMaxPercent": 70,

  // On a CORRECT block (right-side shield or a parry) the blocker's own tiredness counts only
  // this much toward staggering or knocking him down - a correct block breaks him mainly on a
  // BIG mismatch (a peasant's stick against a berserker's axe), so skill pays. 100: his
  // tiredness counts in full, as on a wrong-side block or a clean hit.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "CorrectBlockTiredWeightPercent": 25,

  // How much the BLOCKER's own tiredness lowers the riposte: its chance × (1 − this × his
  // tiredness). 0: a tired man's correct block still makes a tired attacker reel. 100: only a
  // blocker in the green ripostes at full chance, an empty one never.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "RiposteBlockerTiredPercent": 0,

  // How long a stagger lasts on a man in the green, in seconds. It grows with his tiredness by
  // the next setting.
  // (range 0.1 to 3.0)
  "StaggerBaseSeconds": 0.6,

  // An exhausted man's stagger lasts this much longer than a fresh man's (150: 0.6 s fresh, 1.5
  // s empty), in a straight line with his tiredness - and less predictably (the randomness
  // below).
  // (range 0 to 500)
  "StaggerTiredExtraPercent": 150,

  // No stagger lasts longer than this, in seconds, whatever the roll.
  // (range 0.2 to 5.0)
  "StaggerMaxSeconds": 2.0,

  // A kicked or bashed man reels back as in the game, but this much longer when exhausted (150:
  // 2.5 times as long at an empty bar), in a straight line with his tiredness - so a kick gives
  // a tired man's enemy time to strike. A fresh man reels as in the game.
  // (range 0 to 500)
  "KickReelTiredExtraPercent": 150,

  // An exhausted man knocked to the ground takes up to this many times as long to get up (2 =
  // twice as long at an empty bar), in a straight line with his tiredness. 1 = the game's own.
  // (range 1.0 to 4.0)
  "GetUpMaxSlowdown": 2.0,

  // After every block or parry the blocker cannot act for a moment (the game's own stun); an
  // exhausted blocker's lasts this much longer (100: twice as long at an empty bar). 0 (the
  // default since the spike's playtest): the game's own stun - lengthening it changed nothing
  // the engine plays; the stagger is the window.
  // (range 0 to 500)
  "BlockStunTiredExtraPercent": 0,

  // A riposted attacker recoils for up to this many seconds - half of it when he is fresh, all
  // of it when he is empty.
  // (range 0.0 to 3.0)
  "RiposteStunMaxSeconds": 1.0,

  // Every stagger, reel, get-up and stun length is rolled within ± this percent at an EMPTY bar
  // (less as he is fresher, none in the green): a fresh man's stagger is predictable, an
  // exhausted man's is not.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "ImpactRandomPercent": 30,

  // The game caps every block stun at 0.8 s; while the impact system runs it allows up to this
  // many seconds for the stuns it lengthens (every other stun keeps the game's 0.8 s).
  // (range 0.8 to 5.0)
  "ImpactStunCapSeconds": 2.0,

  // After a stagger (or a lengthened reel) ends, the same man cannot be staggered again for
  // this many seconds - nobody is stun-locked to death.
  // (range 0.0 to 20.0)
  "ImpactStaggerImmunitySeconds": 2.0,

  // After a man gets up from a knockdown he cannot be knocked down again for this many seconds.
  // (range 0.0 to 30.0)
  "ImpactKnockdownImmunitySeconds": 5.0,

  // Every stagger, dropped shield or knockdown a man suffered in the last this many seconds
  // makes the next one against him less likely (the factor below). 0 = never.
  // (range 0.0 to 60.0)
  "ImpactDiminishWindowSeconds": 8.0,

  // Each recent impact multiplies the next chance against the same man by this (0.5: one recent
  // impact halves it, two quarter it). 1 = no limit.
  // (range 0.0 to 1.0)
  "ImpactDiminishFactor": 0.5,

  // A dropped shield lies on the ground and can be picked up again the game's way (the AI only
  // when no enemy is within 20 m; you with the use key). Above 0: nobody picks a dropped shield
  // up for this many seconds. 0 = the game's own.
  // (range 0.0 to 120.0)
  "ShieldPickupLockSeconds": 0.0,

  // A rider is never staggered (the horse shares the move); a "knockdown" on a rider knocks him
  // OFF his horse instead, at this percent of the knockdown chance. Horses themselves are the
  // game's own.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "ImpactRiderDismountPercent": 50,

  // The game lets a man shrug off a light blow without flinching; on: a tired man shrugs off
  // less the more tired he is (his flinch threshold falls with his strength), so a clean hit
  // always tells on an exhausted man.
  // (true or false)
  "ImpactTiredNeverShrugsOff": true,

  // Step 52 (Anton: a fresh shock unit charging a tired line must be devastating): the
  // attacker's own speed into the blow - his run or sprint towards the man he strikes - adds to
  // the blow's impact, for kicks, bashes and weapon blows, blocked or not. Riders: their
  // horse's speed, at the rider settings below. Off = only the weapon and the swing count.
  // (true or false)
  "ImpactMomentumEnabled": true,

  // A blow struck at the sprint speed below or faster has this much more impact (60: x1.6 - a
  // sprinting axe-man throws a tired man around); at a walk or slower nothing is added, in
  // between a straight line.
  // (range 0 to 200)
  "ImpactMomentumPercent": 60,

  // Up to this speed into the blow (metres a second) a man adds no momentum - the game's walk
  // is about 1.8 m/s, a run 4-5 m/s.
  // (range 0.0 to 10.0)
  "ImpactMomentumWalkMetresPerSecond": 2.0,

  // From this speed into the blow (metres a second) the whole momentum bonus is added - a fresh
  // man's sprint (step 33) runs about 7-9 m/s, a run 4-5 m/s.
  // (range 0.5 to 20.0)
  "ImpactMomentumSprintMetresPerSecond": 7.0,

  // Step 53: a rider's swing or thrust carries his HORSE's speed into the blow - this much more
  // impact at a full gallop (30: x1.3, half a man's sprint, so a cavalry charge into a tired
  // line throws men down without felling everyone); a couched lance never (it is the game's own
  // big hit already). 0 = riders add nothing.
  // (range 0 to 200)
  "ImpactMomentumRiderPercent": 30,

  // Up to this horse speed into the blow (metres a second) a rider adds no momentum - a horse
  // at a walk; a trot is about 4-5 m/s.
  // (range 0.0 to 20.0)
  "ImpactMomentumRiderWalkMetresPerSecond": 3.0,

  // From this horse speed into the blow (metres a second) a rider adds the whole rider bonus -
  // a good horse gallops at about 9-11 m/s.
  // (range 0.5 to 30.0)
  "ImpactMomentumRiderGallopMetresPerSecond": 10.0,

  // Off: only what happens to you and what you do. On: also when a man of your side knocks an
  // enemy HERO down or off his horse, or when a hero of your side is knocked down or off his
  // horse.
  // (true or false)
  "ImpactMessagesIncludeYourMen": false,

  // The shortest time between two of these lines; what happens meanwhile is merged into the
  // next one ("You knock Aldric down; your shield is knocked away"). 0 = a line for every tick
  // that has something.
  // (range 0.0 to 10.0)
  "ImpactMessageMinSeconds": 1.5,

  // Step 54: when the man an AI soldier fights is reeling from a stagger or lies knocked down
  // (by this impact system - yours too), the soldier presses the opening: he decides to attack
  // as eagerly as the setting below for as long as it lasts (+ a short grace), and a timid man
  // close to him steps in for it. Both sides; never you (you punish with your own hands). Off =
  // the AI ignores the openings.
  // (true or false)
  "ImpactPunishEnabled": true,

  // How eagerly an AI soldier decides to attack a reeling or downed enemy, as a share of the
  // game's own AI (100 = the game's full eagerness; the aggression setting's 60% fresh / 20%
  // empty and a fever's 80% are raised to it, never lowered).
  // (range 0 to 200)
  "ImpactPunishAggressionPercent": 100,

  // The opening lasts this much longer than the stagger or the time on the ground - a swing
  // started just as he recovers still counts.
  // (range 0.0 to 3.0)
  "ImpactPunishGraceSeconds": 0.5,

  // A TIMID soldier (courage) whose enemy reels or lies down within this many metres of him
  // steps in for the opening, like a surge - brave until it closes. Farther away he keeps his
  // distance. 0 = timid men never do.
  // (range 0.0 to 10.0)
  "ImpactPunishRangeMetres": 3.0,

  // The game lets a man shrug a light blow off (no reaction at all) BEFORE it asks whether he
  // falls - so a knockdown decided on such a blow was lost. On: the blow is decided first, and
  // a knockdown or stagger refuses the shrug-off, so it plays. Off: the game's shrug-off wins
  // (as before step 62).
  // (true or false)
  "ImpactShrugOffYieldsToImpact": true,

  // If a knockdown decided on a landed blow (a kick, a bash, a clean hit) has not started to
  // play within this many seconds, the man is knocked down by a blow of our own - once. 0 = no
  // backup.
  // (range 0.0 to 3.0)
  "ImpactFallBackupSeconds": 0.5,

  // How much both men's TOUGHNESS - armour, rank and the health left, the courage settings'
  // measure - weighs in who staggers or knocks down whom: the mismatch × (attacker's toughness
  // ÷ defender's) to this power. 0.5: a legionary (4.4 times as tough as a looter) hits as if
  // twice as strong, and the looter's blows on him half as strong. 0 = only tiredness, weapons
  // and skill count.
  // (range 0.0 to 2.0)
  "ImpactToughnessWeight": 0.5,

  // A blow that lands on a man holding a bow, crossbow or sling counts this much stronger -
  // both hands busy, no guard (130: x1.3). 100 = like anyone.
  // (range 100 to 300)
  "ImpactRangedInHandPercent": 130,

  // A blow that lands on a man from BEHIND counts this much stronger toward staggering or
  // knocking him down (200: twice) - a well-led charge into the back of a unit throws men to
  // the ground. 100 = like a blow from the front.
  // (range 100 to 500)
  "ImpactRearPercent": 200,

  // A blow that lands on a man from the SIDE counts this much stronger (140: x1.4). 100 = like
  // a blow from the front.
  // (range 100 to 500)
  "ImpactFlankPercent": 140,

  // A blow counts as from behind when the attacker stands more than this many degrees from
  // where the man faces (120: the back third of a circle).
  // (range 90 to 180)
  "ImpactRearDegrees": 120,

  // A blow counts as from the side from this many degrees off his facing up to the 'from
  // behind' angle (60: between 60 and 120). Never above the 'from behind' angle.
  // (range 0 to 180)
  "ImpactFlankDegrees": 60,

  // A man who was sprinting strikes his first blow within this many seconds after the sprint as
  // a CHARGE - its full momentum (and the full damage roll, if that switch is on), even though
  // he slowed down to swing (the AI's sprint ends a few metres from the enemy). Only the first
  // blow; while he still sprints, every blow. 0 = only a blow struck while sprinting.
  // (range 0.0 to 5.0)
  "ImpactChargeCarrySeconds": 1.5,

  // A CHARGING man (sprinting into the blow) whose blow is blocked on the RIGHT side of a
  // shield can be thrown to the ground - at most this chance, for a full sprint by a weaker or
  // tired man into a fresh, tougher shieldman; nothing for a walking attacker (he only reels).
  // You too. 0 = never.
  // (range 0 to 100)
  "RiposteKnockdownMaxPercent": 40,

  // Where the thrown-back chance starts on the pressure scale of the riposte (0 = any mismatch
  // against the charger counts, 1 = an empty, outmatched attacker). The other curves: a stagger
  // from 0, a knockdown from 0.35.
  // (range 0.0 to 0.95)
  "RiposteKnockdownFrom": 0.0,

  // On a right-side block or a parry, the attacker's own speed into the blow is turned against
  // him - the riposte (he reels, or is thrown back) counts this much more at a full sprint
  // (100: twice). 0 = his speed does not count on a correct block.
  // (range 0 to 300)
  "RiposteMomentumPercent": 100,

  // How much an outmatched man suffers: every doubling of the mismatch beyond the even band
  // adds this to the pressure on him (0.25: an enemy four times stronger counts as much as
  // being about a third tired). 0 = only tiredness counts.
  // (range 0.0 to 2.0)
  "ImpactMismatchWeight": 0.25,

  // A mismatch within this many doublings either way counts as an even match (0.5 = a factor of
  // 1.41) - so two fresh men of a kind never stagger each other. Only the part beyond it adds
  // pressure (or takes pressure away, for the weaker attacker).
  // (range 0.0 to 3.0)
  "ImpactEvenBandDoublings": 0.5,

  // Body strength = his CURRENT Athletics points to this power (0.5: four times the points =
  // twice the body). A 200-point king at full strength against a 50-point man at 20% is 4.5
  // times the body. 0 = Athletics points do not count, only tiredness.
  // (range 0.0 to 2.0)
  "ImpactBodyExponent": 0.5,

  // An empty man still has a body: his body strength never counts fewer points than this.
  // (range 1 to 200)
  "ImpactBodyFloorPoints": 10,

  // A man still reeling from a stagger or a lengthened reel of this system gets this much extra
  // pressure: a kick very likely knocks him down, even a weapon blow can. A fresh man's
  // ordinary flinch does not count.
  // (range 0.0 to 3.0)
  "ImpactStaggeredBonus": 0.75,

  // A blow that lands adds this times the share of his full health it took (1: a blow that
